+ * the id/cookie the service returns.  The calls are asynchronous, so a release
+ * can arrive while the request is still in flight.  The original code looked
+ * the id up at release time, found none ("was never requested"), did nothing,
+ * and then stored the id when the reply came in -- a lock that nothing would
+ * ever clear.  For the system state that kept repowerd from ever suspending
+ * again until media-hub restarted; it happens whenever a client disconnects
+ * or stops right after starting playback.
+ *
+ * So instead each interface records what is *wanted*, allows one call in
+ * flight at a time, and when that call completes brings the service in line
+ * with whatever is wanted by then.
+ */
